      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Pose 3:\nLaying down on the side with hands on the ground in front. (Legacy pictured 1st)\nThis pose is the most glaring one. before the wrist rotation allowed you to position the elbow in a more relaxed pose, but now the avoidance system is acting very aggressive and forcing the elbow away from the body in a very unnatural way, and no matter of wrist movement can change this position. I can see this being a concern for users that like to relax or sleep on their side.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
